DATA (web hook composition, bound via shared P1/S8 state-holders — no HTTP in the view):
  useVehicles (default vehicle id) + useClimateHistory(vid) -> GET /climate?vehicle_id=  (raw SI JSON array)
  useUnits (SI->display temp at the render boundary) + useDateFormat (axis labels) + useTranslation (i18n)
  Decode: each row's timestamp = created_at ?? timestamp; SI inside_temp / outside_temp (degC, nullable);
  rows without a timestamp dropped; sorted chronologically (web .filter(...).sort(...)).

STATES (every state renders — no hidden surfaces):
  loading  -> StatGridSkeleton(2) + chart skeleton (a11y "Loading")
  content  -> title + Cabin/Outside latest stat row + 2-series gradient area chart (inside warm / outside blue)
              + Cabin/Outside legend
  empty    -> "No climate history" EmptyState (ThermometerSun) — web isEmpty={!hasData}
  error    -> honest: empty body + freshness offline chip + refresh retry (web passes no WidgetShell error)
  stale/offline -> cached chart kept visible, freshness chip flagged, auto-retry via DataFreshness
  compact (cols<=1) -> stat row only, no title/chart (web compact branch)

i18n (P1/S10; keys already present in app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml):
  translation_widget_climateHistory_{title,cabin,outside,noData}, translation_common_{refresh,loading,offline},
  translation_a11y_loading, translation_freshness_{justNow,seconds,minutes,hours,days,weeks}. No English literals.

Registry (web registry/climate.ts): id "climate-history", category "climate", default 2x4, min 2x4, max 4x40
  (ClimateHistoryRegistration; unit-tested isWithinBounds/clamp). Same ID + size constraints as web.

a11y: header title carries heading(); each stat cell merges a "label, value+unit" description; the loading
  skeleton + refresh control carry TalkBack names; font scale + light/dark via Material 3 tokens (P1/S9).

Telemetry: one-shot view.opened with slug "ClimateHistoryWidget" (P1/S11), PII-safe (no temperature payload).

